<!DOCTYPE html>
{#
  Base page shell for every Yolo layout.

  Two variants, selected by `bare`:
    full - sidebar, site header and search (posts, single-page index)
    bare - content only (hub index, hub post listing)

  Leaf layouts pick a variant through front matter:
    isHub: true        always bare        (layouts/hub.njk)
    isIndexPage: true  bare in hub mode   (layouts/index.njk)
    neither            always full        (layouts/post.njk)
#}
{% set bare = isHub or (isIndexPage and settings.hub.enabled) %}
{#
  Opt-in CSS/JS for this page. Single-page mode renders another post's body as
  the home page, and front matter does not travel with the body, so take that
  post's ext_css/ext_js too - otherwise its demos render but stay inert.
#}
{% set pageExtCss = ext_css %}
{% set pageExtJs = ext_js %}
{% if isIndexPage and not settings.hub.enabled %}
  {% set headline = collections.postsRanked | first %}
  {% set pageExtCss = headline.data.ext_css %}
  {% set pageExtJs = headline.data.ext_js %}
{% endif %}
<html lang="en" class="yolo-themed">
{% include "components/head.njk" %}
{#
  The sidebar is not part of the bare/full split. A site that configures one
  gets it everywhere, the hub index included - same width, same style, same
  toggle. What differs is what it holds: the hub has no headings worth an
  index, so there it carries the logo alone (see components/sidebar.njk).
#}
<body id="yolo-site"{% if settings.sidebar %} class="sidebar-{{ settings.sidebar.position | default('left') }}"{% endif %}>
  {% if settings.sidebar %}
  {#
    The sidebar is open or collapsed because you last left it that way, the
    hub and every page alike. Posts used to arrive collapsed on a ?from=hub
    flag instead, which fought the hub's own sidebar and shifted the column
    on every link.

    This runs here, before the sidebar is parsed, for the same reason
    theme.js runs in <head>: settle it ahead of the first paint and there is
    nothing to animate and nothing to see. Deciding it on DOMContentLoaded
    paints the sidebar open and then yanks it away.
  #}
  <script>
    try {
      if (localStorage.getItem('yolo-sidebar') === 'hidden') {
        document.body.classList.add('sidebar-hidden');
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  </script>
  {% include "components/sidebar.njk" %}
  {% endif %}
  {% include "components/sticky-controls.njk" %}
  <div id="yolo-container" class="container {{ settings.align | default('left') }}">
    {% if not bare %}
    <header>
      {% include "components/header.njk" %}
    </header>
    {% include "components/search.njk" %}
    {% endif %}
    <main{% if not bare %} style="clear: both"{% endif %}>
      <div id="page-content" class="page-content">
        {{ content | safe }}
      </div>
    </main>
    <footer>
      {% include "components/footer.njk" %}
    </footer>
  </div>
  {% include "components/scripts.njk" %}
</body>
</html>
